From 12cbe9c71378c2fd7785b8027f4032ee928c5d6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:53:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] ARM64: configs: Amber: Enable CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL

Android 12 bpfloader needs bpf() to create the tethering maps; without
it the critical tethering object fails (-ENOSYS) and init reboots with
'bpfloader-failed'. Programs requiring newer kernels are skipped.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_Amber_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_Amber_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_Amber_defconfig
index 93f3b8c8..e6b5c560 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_Amber_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_Amber_defconfig
@@ -708,3 +708,4 @@ CONFIG_PSTORE=y
 CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
 CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG=y
 CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y
+CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y
-- 
2.56.0

